  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cities for Enhanced Governance and Engagement (CHANGE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Philippines):  .USAID, through the CHANGE activity, promotes collective actions and stronger partnerships between local government units (LGUs) and citizens to strengthen democratic governance. It complements portfolio-wide initiatives to disperse development outside of the capital. ..USAID will strengthen the enabling environment for decentralization by building on the results of the activity&apos;s review of the Local Government Code of the Philippines. This will include steps to identify gaps and build the constituency for policy reform. USAID will conduct case studies to demonstrate the implementation of the local devolution process by LGUs and national government agencies, as indicated in Devolution Transition Plans, and will help strengthen local planning systems and processes to improve the quality of local development plans, public investment programs, and resource mobilization...To promote local government transparency and accountability, USAID will assist LGUs to develop participatory mechanisms to engage citizens in governance processes and provide constituents with access to official records such as LGU plans, regular fiscal disclosures, and Statement of Receipts and Expenditures reports. USAID will strengthen the ability of LGUs to respond to citizen requests, provide access to information, improve the management of local resources and foster community participation in the delivery of public services. USAID will also promote citizen participation and oversight of local governance processes. USAID will assess the capacity needs of civil society organizations (CSOs) and deliver training on topics such as citizen feedback mechanisms, to bolster the effectiveness of CSOs in holding local governments accountable. USAID will support grants to strengthen networking and citizen-led initiatives. Finally, USAID will maximize entry points for the promotion of good governance practices by integrating participatory governance criteria into key award and incentives progr</narrative>
  </description>
